00:14:32.456 --> 00:14:34.165
Good afternoon,

00:14:32.456 --> 00:14:34.165
I'm Brian Williams.

00:14:34.207 --> 00:14:37.127
Our top story, an accidental

00:14:34.207 --> 00:14:37.127
space shuttle launch

00:14:37.168 --> 00:14:39.588
that has sent a Rhode Island

00:14:37.168 --> 00:14:39.588
family into orbit.

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:42.006
For more on the story,

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:42.006
we go to our local affiliate

00:14:42.048 --> 00:14:44.342
Channel Five Quahog where

00:14:42.048 --> 00:14:44.342
Tom Tucker is on the scene.

00:14:44.384 --> 00:14:45.343
Tom?

00:14:45.385 --> 00:14:46.595
Thanks, Brian.

00:14:46.637 --> 00:14:48.430
I, uh, saw that you opened

00:14:46.637 --> 00:14:48.430
my birthday Evite.

00:14:48.472 --> 00:14:51.141
Now I just need you

00:14:48.472 --> 00:14:51.141
to go ahead and reply.

00:14:51.182 --> 00:14:53.017
I'm standing here at the home

00:14:51.182 --> 00:14:53.017
of the Griffin family,

00:14:53.059 --> 00:14:54.394
chatting with their neighbors.

00:14:54.436 --> 00:14:55.979
So, the Griffins

00:14:54.436 --> 00:14:55.979
might be dead.

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:57.314
How does that

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:57.314
make you feel?

00:14:57.355 --> 00:14:59.983
Griffin dead?

00:14:57.355 --> 00:14:59.983
I take.

00:15:02.611 --> 00:15:04.112
No, no, they

00:15:02.611 --> 00:15:04.112
might be dead.

00:15:04.154 --> 00:15:05.739
They also might

00:15:04.154 --> 00:15:05.739
still be alive.

00:15:05.781 --> 00:15:07.825
It's okay, I-I take.

00:15:07.866 --> 00:15:09.868
(loud rumbling)

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:13.204
(loud popping)

00:15:18.042 --> 00:15:19.837
Peter, what are you doing?

00:15:19.878 --> 00:15:21.421
I'm going out for

00:15:19.878 --> 00:15:21.421
a space walk, Lois.

00:15:21.463 --> 00:15:23.006
You know, this

00:15:21.463 --> 00:15:23.006
is our one chance

00:15:23.047 --> 00:15:25.175
to experience the

00:15:23.047 --> 00:15:25.175
awe-inspiring wonders

00:15:25.216 --> 00:15:26.885
of space firsthand.

00:15:30.681 --> 00:15:33.057
Wow, neat.

00:15:33.099 --> 00:15:35.018
So, this is space.

00:15:42.025 --> 00:15:44.068
Damn it.

00:15:45.737 --> 00:15:48.365
(girl laughing)

00:15:48.406 --> 00:15:51.034
Ha! Stupid drunk bitches.

00:15:53.537 --> 00:15:54.621
Hey, Brian, check it out.

00:15:54.663 --> 00:15:56.414
Meg's poking

00:15:54.663 --> 00:15:56.414
around the cargo hold.

00:15:56.456 --> 00:15:58.291
I'm gonna give her

00:15:56.456 --> 00:15:58.291
a little scare.

00:16:08.719 --> 00:16:10.053
(sniffs)

00:16:10.053 --> 00:16:12.305
Aw, boy, I think

00:16:10.053 --> 00:16:12.305
this space food has gone bad.

00:16:12.347 --> 00:16:14.265
Peter, that's a

00:16:12.347 --> 00:16:14.265
fecal collection bag.

00:16:14.307 --> 00:16:15.433
Oh, there's a bag for that?

00:16:15.475 --> 00:16:17.060
'Cause mine's over there

00:16:15.475 --> 00:16:17.060
twirling in the air

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:18.562
like a slow baton.

00:16:18.603 --> 00:16:21.481
STEWIE:

00:16:18.603 --> 00:16:21.481
Well, someone's got to lead

00:16:18.603 --> 00:16:21.481
this marching band. Ew!

00:16:21.523 --> 00:16:22.816
MAN (over radio):

00:16:21.523 --> 00:16:22.816
Griffins come in.

00:16:22.858 --> 00:16:24.401
Yes! Yes, we're here.

00:16:24.442 --> 00:16:26.152
Well, I have some good news.

00:16:26.194 --> 00:16:28.739
The autopilot is capable

00:16:26.194 --> 00:16:28.739
of taking you home.

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:30.114
But guys...

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:30.114
(static crackling)

00:16:30.156 --> 00:16:31.449
...to engage, we're gonna...

00:16:31.491 --> 00:16:33.243
...to take the shuttle out of...

00:16:33.284 --> 00:16:34.828
(radio goes silent)

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:35.913
Hello?

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:35.913
(static drones)

00:16:35.954 --> 00:16:38.122
Hello?

00:16:35.954 --> 00:16:38.122
Crap, I think we lost him.

00:16:38.164 --> 00:16:39.541
Let me fix that.

00:16:39.583 --> 00:16:42.126
If radio deejays have taught me

00:16:39.583 --> 00:16:42.126
anything about radio,

00:16:42.168 --> 00:16:43.211
it's that you got

00:16:42.168 --> 00:16:43.211
to do two things.

00:16:43.253 --> 00:16:45.547
Turn it up and rip the knob off.

00:16:45.589 --> 00:16:47.257
Peter, no!

00:16:45.589 --> 00:16:47.257
(crackling)

00:16:47.298 --> 00:16:49.217
Damn it, now we've lost

00:16:47.298 --> 00:16:49.217
communication entirely.

00:16:49.259 --> 00:16:50.427
What are we gonna do?

00:16:50.468 --> 00:16:52.136
I don't know,

00:16:50.468 --> 00:16:52.136
but we got to try something.

00:16:52.178 --> 00:16:53.513
If we don't get this shuttle

00:16:52.178 --> 00:16:53.513
out of orbit soon,

00:16:53.555 --> 00:16:55.432
we're gonna

00:16:53.555 --> 00:16:55.432
run out of oxygen and die.

00:16:55.473 --> 00:16:56.641
Is failure an option?

00:16:56.683 --> 00:16:57.851
No, it's not.

00:16:57.893 --> 00:16:59.269
Aw, that was my suggestion.

00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:01.145
All right, come on, everyone,

00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:01.145
we got to put our heads

00:17:01.187 --> 00:17:02.355
together

00:17:01.187 --> 00:17:02.355
and try to find a solution.

00:17:02.397 --> 00:17:04.190
Don't worry-- Griffins

00:17:02.397 --> 00:17:04.190
have a long history

00:17:04.232 --> 00:17:05.275
of figuring stuff out.

00:17:05.316 --> 00:17:06.568
Like my great-grandfather

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:08.486
who invented the

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:08.486
first marital aid.

00:17:11.155 --> 00:17:13.283
This gives me an idea.

00:17:16.286 --> 00:17:17.704
She's dead.

00:17:20.582 --> 00:17:22.125
All right, come on,

00:17:20.582 --> 00:17:22.125
if mission control thought

00:17:22.125 --> 00:17:23.167
we could help get the shuttle

00:17:22.125 --> 00:17:23.167
out of orbit,

00:17:23.209 --> 00:17:24.544
it can't be that hard.

00:17:24.586 --> 00:17:26.004
Okay, okay,

00:17:24.586 --> 00:17:26.004
uh, try this.

00:17:26.129 --> 00:17:27.338
Hit up, up, down, down,

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:29.674
left, right, left, right,

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:29.674
B, A, start.

00:17:29.716 --> 00:17:30.968
Then we'll have

00:17:29.716 --> 00:17:30.968
unlimited lives.

00:17:31.009 --> 00:17:32.803
Come on,

00:17:31.009 --> 00:17:32.803
we're running out of time.

00:17:32.844 --> 00:17:34.888
Oh, Meg, all your suicide

00:17:32.844 --> 00:17:34.888
threats over the years,

00:17:34.930 --> 00:17:37.724
and you're just as chicken

00:17:34.930 --> 00:17:37.724
(bleep) as the rest of us.

00:17:37.766 --> 00:17:40.602
Hey, guys, I think I have

00:17:37.766 --> 00:17:40.602
an idea that could help us.

00:17:40.644 --> 00:17:43.229
In Space Camp, we learned about

00:17:40.644 --> 00:17:43.229
countering forward momentum

00:17:43.271 --> 00:17:44.773
with retro rockets.

00:17:44.815 --> 00:17:47.191
If we use them now,

00:17:44.815 --> 00:17:47.191
the ship might slow down enough

00:17:47.233 --> 00:17:50.153
for gravity

00:17:47.233 --> 00:17:50.153
to pull us out of orbit.

00:17:50.194 --> 00:17:53.239
PETER: That's an egg that I

00:17:50.194 --> 00:17:53.239
hucked at you for being a nerd.

00:17:55.158 --> 00:17:57.160
Chris, if you think it'll help,

00:17:55.158 --> 00:17:57.160
just try it!

00:18:00.998 --> 00:18:03.333
Ah, we're slowing down.

00:18:00.998 --> 00:18:03.333
That's a good sign.

00:18:03.374 --> 00:18:05.335
You know, what's not slowing

00:18:03.374 --> 00:18:05.335
down--<i> Breaking Bad.</i>

00:18:05.376 --> 00:18:07.504
Haven't seen anything like it

00:18:05.376 --> 00:18:07.504
since<i> The Wire.</i>

00:18:07.545 --> 00:18:09.631
God, he never shuts up

00:18:07.545 --> 00:18:09.631
about those shows.

00:18:09.673 --> 00:18:10.715
Oh, my God!

00:18:10.757 --> 00:18:12.550
I think it might be working!

00:18:12.592 --> 00:18:14.177
(screaming)

00:18:14.218 --> 00:18:15.762
BRIAN:

00:18:14.218 --> 00:18:15.762
We're spinning out!

00:18:18.473 --> 00:18:20.224
MEG:

00:18:18.473 --> 00:18:20.224
Oh, my God,

00:18:18.473 --> 00:18:20.224
we're gonna die!

00:18:20.266 --> 00:18:21.852
There's so many things

00:18:20.266 --> 00:18:21.852
I didn't do.

00:18:21.893 --> 00:18:23.394
I never got to go to college!

00:18:23.436 --> 00:18:26.023
My book wasn't all

00:18:23.436 --> 00:18:26.023
I wanted it to be in spots!

00:18:26.064 --> 00:18:28.274
Peter, I wanted to

00:18:26.064 --> 00:18:28.274
grow old with you!

00:18:28.316 --> 00:18:29.776
Well, you kind of did.

00:18:29.818 --> 00:18:31.903
I never got to wear it better!

00:18:35.615 --> 00:18:38.576
(grunts)

00:18:35.615 --> 00:18:38.576
I have to reorient

00:18:35.615 --> 00:18:38.576
the retro rockets

00:18:38.618 --> 00:18:40.871
to counter the spin rotation!

00:18:42.664 --> 00:18:44.332
(grunts)

00:19:01.224 --> 00:19:02.433
Chris, what are you doing?

00:19:02.475 --> 00:19:04.019
(dramatically):

00:19:02.475 --> 00:19:04.019
Saving our lives.

00:19:04.061 --> 00:19:05.562
Aw, I wish he

00:19:04.061 --> 00:19:05.562
hadn't said that.

00:19:05.603 --> 00:19:07.271
Now I'm kind of

00:19:05.603 --> 00:19:07.271
rooting against him.

00:19:10.859 --> 00:19:12.819
We're straightening out!

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:16.280
Ah, look! It says

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:16.280
"autopilot engaged."

00:19:16.322 --> 00:19:18.658
Good for him.

00:19:16.322 --> 00:19:18.658
I'm glad he found someone.

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:20.451
Oh, thank God,

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:20.451
we're saved!

00:19:20.493 --> 00:19:24.081
I can't believe I got to go

00:19:20.493 --> 00:19:24.081
to space before Derek Watson.

00:19:24.122 --> 00:19:25.373
Who's Derek Watson?

00:19:25.415 --> 00:19:27.042
Nobody now.

00:19:42.557 --> 00:19:44.267
They've re-entered

00:19:42.557 --> 00:19:44.267
the atmosphere!

00:19:44.308 --> 00:19:47.020
(cheering)

00:19:47.062 --> 00:19:49.522
I'm not cheering.

00:19:47.062 --> 00:19:49.522
I don't even know them.

00:19:57.739 --> 00:19:59.616
(tires screech)

00:19:59.657 --> 00:20:02.744
(cheering)

00:20:11.544 --> 00:20:14.422
(cheering,

00:20:11.544 --> 00:20:14.422
camera shutter clicking)

00:20:16.549 --> 00:20:18.342
Well, thanks to

00:20:16.549 --> 00:20:18.342
no gravity in space,

00:20:18.384 --> 00:20:21.429
my spine stretched and I am

00:20:18.384 --> 00:20:21.429
now a confident six, three,

00:20:21.471 --> 00:20:24.474
so, Lois, I will be leaving you

00:20:21.471 --> 00:20:24.474
for a hotter woman.

00:20:24.515 --> 00:20:27.435
Never mind, Lois,

00:20:24.515 --> 00:20:27.435
I love you so much.

00:20:30.814 --> 00:20:33.858
Chris, our family is alive

00:20:30.814 --> 00:20:33.858
right now because of you.

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:35.110
You saved us.

00:20:35.152 --> 00:20:36.402
That's right, buddy.

00:20:36.444 --> 00:20:38.362
It was your brains

00:20:36.444 --> 00:20:38.362
that pulled us through.

00:20:38.404 --> 00:20:40.657
We're so sorry

00:20:38.404 --> 00:20:40.657
we ever doubted you.

00:20:40.698 --> 00:20:41.950
Thanks, you guys.

00:20:41.992 --> 00:20:43.076
You bet, champ.

00:20:43.118 --> 00:20:45.120
Hey, by the way,

00:20:43.118 --> 00:20:45.120
who moved our house?